Chapter: PicEoiByVector
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 While the tick counter reads 48, `spin-until` holds 48 in RAX, the local
 timer's vector. A PIT tick taken there must still be acknowledged to the PIC:
 a kernel that picks the chip from the interrupted RAX (COMPILER-104) sends it
 to the local APIC, IRQ0 stays in service, the counter stops at 48, and this
 never prints.

Section: Body

  spin-until : Integer -> Integer
  spin-until (deadline) =
    if get-ticks >= deadline then deadline
    else spin-until deadline

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("reached : " & show (spin-until 60))
  end
